Delete a network and take its address off the interface.

Any address range served on this network stops validating, and `olr dhcp`
will say so against its own field the next time it is applied. Remove the
range first if you mean to stop serving cleanly.

Usage:
  olr net rm <name> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for rm

Global Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would change and exit without applying it
  -o, --output string   output format: text|json (default "text")
      --socket string   olrd control socket (default "/run/olr/olrd.sock")
